---
import { agents } from "../../../lib/agents";
import Everywhere from "../everywhere.astro";

// Excerpts of what `ultracite init --linter bun` writes for editors, which
// are the Oxlint provider's settings (packages/cli/src/data/editors.ts), and
// lines from a real `bunx ultracite check` under a coding agent on Bun
// 1.4.4-canary.1, which prints Oxlint's compact agent format (the benchmark
// fixture and the button component, help text left out).
const vscodeSettings = `{
  "[typescriptreact]": {
    "editor.defaultFormatter": "oxc.oxc-vscode"
  },
  "editor.codeActionsOnSave": {
    "source.fixAll.oxc": "explicit"
  },
  "editor.formatOnSave": true
}`;

const zedSettings = `"oxlint": {
  "initialization_options": {
    "settings": {
      "run": "onType",
      "typeAware": true,
      "unusedDisableDirectives": "deny"
    }
  }
}`;

const diagnostics = [
  {
    location: "components/button.tsx:5:8",
    message: "Expected a function expression.",
    rule: "eslint(func-style)",
  },
  {
    location: "src/data.ts:20:14",
    message: "Use `Array#toSorted()` instead of `Array#sort()`.",
    rule: "unicorn(no-array-sort)",
  },
  {
    location: "src/store.ts:1:22",
    message:
      "Prefer using a top-level type-only import instead of inline type specifiers.",
    rule: "import(consistent-type-specifier-style)",
  },
  {
    location: "src/utils.ts:5:54",
    message: "Object keys should be sorted",
    rule: "eslint(sort-keys)",
  },
  {
    location: "src/utils.ts:59:14",
    message: "Unexpected `await` inside a loop.",
    rule: "eslint(no-await-in-loop)",
  },
];
---

<Everywhere
  cards={[
    {
      body: "Bun has no language server, so the Oxc extension lints and formats on save with Oxlint and Oxfmt, reading the same two configs. `init` installs both packages when it sets up an editor.",
      code: { lang: "jsonc", path: ".vscode/settings.json", text: vscodeSettings },
      eyebrow: "VS Code, Cursor, Devin Desktop",
      title: "Your editor runs Oxlint",
    },
    {
      body: "Zed’s Oxc extension checks each keystroke with the type-aware rules on. Keep rule changes in `oxlint.config.ts`: the extension doesn’t read `bunfig.toml`.",
      code: { lang: "jsonc", path: ".zed/settings.json", text: zedSettings },
      eyebrow: "Zed",
      title: "Lint as you type",
    },
    {
      body: `\`bun lint\` prints Oxlint’s compact format when a coding agent runs it, one line per problem. \`init\` also writes the rules into \`AGENTS.md\`, which all ${agents.length} agents read.`,
      eyebrow: "Coding agents and CI",
      title: "Output written for agents",
    },
  ]}
  id="bn-everywhere"
  title="Bun on the command line, Oxlint in the editor"
>
  The CLI runs Bun’s tools and your editor runs Oxlint’s, on the same two
  files. <code class="font-mono text-base">ultracite/bun</code> leaves out
  the same rules for both, so they check for the same things.
  <Fragment slot="terminal">
    <p class="mb-1 truncate text-panel-foreground">
      <span class="text-signal">$</span> bunx ultracite check
    </p>
    {
      diagnostics.map((line) => (
        <p class="truncate">
          {line.location}: <span class="text-signal">error</span>{" "}
          <span class="text-panel-foreground">{line.rule}</span>:{" "}
          {line.message}
        </p>
      ))
    }
  </Fragment>
</Everywhere>
